/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (The DBMS Project Presentation and Evaluation Event was organized to provide 3rd-year students with a hands-on platform to exhibit their understanding of database systems and convert theoretical knowledge into practical solutions. Students developed a wide range of projects incorporating essential DBMS elements such as ER modeling, normalization, relational schema design, SQL queries, triggers, and backend integration. Each team presented the problem statement, workflow, database structure, and live project demonstration, showcasing creativity and technical effort.)
/E (The DBMS Project Presentation and Evaluation Event was organized to provide 3rd-year students with a hands-on platform to exhibit their understanding of database systems and convert theoretical knowledge into practical solutions. Students developed a wide range of projects incorporating essential DBMS elements such as ER modeling, normalization, relational schema design, SQL queries, triggers, and backend integration. Each team presented the problem statement, workflow, database structure, and live project demonstration, showcasing creativity and technical effort.)
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [6]
>>
